<div>
  <ProjectHeader title="daedalus" subtitle="Maze generation algorithms" logo={StandardEbooksLogo} custommargin="6px" link="https://maticstric.github.io/daedalus/" />
  <p>
    Daedalus is a website built with React which showcases different algorithms for maze generation with adjustable maze size and ability to step and play through the generation.
    It includes the following algorithms: Randomized Depth First Search, Randomized Kruskal’s Algorithm, Randomized Prim’s Algorithm, and Wilson’s Algorithm.
  </p>
  <p>
    I love finding interesting algorithms with cool visualizations.
    I first encountered randomized depth first search as a maze generation algorithm in high school but was dissapointed by its long, intersection-less corridors — they were too easy to solve!
    This inspired me to learn about more sophisticated algorithms that generate non-biased, perfect mazes.
  </p>
</div>